    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal build for LawDog centers on leveraging favorable matchups against high-xERA arms to maximize counting stats. The primary engine of the lineup is **Lawrence Butler**, whose score of 74.61 stands as our ceiling play against Zack Littell; the combination of a positive park factor and a substantial +13% platoon boost makes him an essential start. Similarly, **Tyler Freeman** (70.13) provides massive value despite his assumed #8 spot in the order, as his high-efficiency matchup against Lowder and a +14% park adjustment solidify his place as an anchor for this afternoon's efficiency floor. We are also banking on **Gavin Sheets** (63.91) to exploit the 4.99 xERA of Dobnak, utilizing a strong SP-skill matchup to drive production from the middle of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup today involved the bench, where **Luis Arraez** (52.45) fell just short of inclusion. While his assumed leadoff spot provides a +10% order bonus, the negative park factor and the presence of the elite Bryan Woo (3.62 xERA) kept his efficiency score below our threshold, favoring the higher offensive upside of our outfield cluster. Meanwhile, we remain wary of the volatility surrounding our lineup constructions, as nearly every slot relies on pending official reports. Specifically, keep an eye on **Jonathan Aranda**; while he didn't crack the daily lineup, he remains a high-variance asset, though his status is further complicated by a 39% rain risk that necessitates caution if considering late-swap maneuvers. \n\nWe are avoiding exposure to elite arms where possible, though **Bryce Harper** (60.59) is a notable exception. Despite facing a tough 3.81 xERA in Sean Manaea, his elite xwOBA metrics and the inherent power profile allow him to remain in the UTIL spot. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Masyn Winn** (59.10), as his value is buoyed by an 86% success rate against the delivery timing of Brandon Pfaadt, making him a sneaky play for the stolen base category, which remains our highest priority in this 5x5 format.",
